From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] secur32: SASL profile functions

SaslEnumerateProfiles{A,W} list the profiles GSS-SPNEGO, GSSAPI and DIGEST-MD5 as a multi-string; SaslGetProfilePackage{A,W} map a profile (case-insensitively) to its SSPI package (Negotiate, Kerberos, WDigest); SaslIdentifyPackage{A,W} pick the best package from a server's mechanism list; SaslInitializeSecurityContext{A,W} and SaslAcceptSecurityContext run the SSPI exchange of the credential's package.
---
--- a/dlls/secur32/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/secur32/Makefile.in
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@ UNIX_CFLAGS  = $(GNUTLS_CFLAGS)
 SOURCES = \
 	lsa.c \
 	negotiate.c \
+	sasl.c \
 	schannel.c \
 	schannel_gnutls.c \
 	secur32.c \
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/secur32/sasl.c
@@ -0,0 +1,290 @@
